WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
Picture two factories making the
same product for British buyers.

2
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:09.230
In Country X, wages are just
one-sixth of wages in the UK.

3
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.740
Yet each unit delivered from
Country X costs 10 pence more.

4
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.720
So why do firms make goods on the other

5
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.050
side of the world?

6
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.400
And why do they then sell them
differently in each country?

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.770
In this mission, you'll sort
out offshoring and outsourcing

8
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.820
with one simple grid.

9
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:28.310
Then you'll place firms
on a line from same

10
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.280
everywhere to adapted for each country.

11
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.610
Your mission: explain why firms go global,

12
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.490
and how they decide what
to change in each market.
